# Cursor Prompt: Two-Page Spread Layout

## Goal
Update `FlipbookViewer` to display entries as a two-page book spread.

## Layout Rules
- Container is always double-page width (two pages side by side), fixed
- **Cover and back cover**: single page centered in the double-width container, other half is empty
- **All middle spreads**: two entries side by side, left and right
- **Odd number of entries**: last spread shows one entry on the left, blank white page on the right. The blank page should have a subtle decorative flourish or faint watermark — not just empty white

## Spread Index Logic
Build a `getSpreads(entries)` helper that chunks entries into spreads:
- `spreads[0]` = cover (single)
- `spreads[1..n-1]` = pairs of entries, padding with `null` if odd
- `spreads[n]` = back cover (single)

The existing prev/next navigation and keyboard controls advance by spread, not by individual page.

## Animation
Keep the existing Framer Motion slide transition as-is. It already operates on the whole spread so no changes needed there.

## Responsive
On mobile (< 640px), drop back to single-page view regardless of spread position — double spreads are too small to be readable on narrow screens.